    <item>
      <title>Forged In FreeCAD: A beginners Keyring and Candlestick</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-a-beginners-keyring-and-candlestick/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 27 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-a-beginners-keyring-and-candlestick/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;image-with-popover&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;figure&gt;&#xA;        &lt;button aria-label=&#34;Zoom image&#34; popovertarget=&#34;img-001&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;img srcset=&#34;https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-a-beginners-keyring-and-candlestick/CAD_1_hu_e39f45ee79e35a30.webp 500w, https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-a-beginners-keyring-and-candlestick/CAD_1_hu_c6dacc2c5e4b6283.webp 1000w, https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-a-beginners-keyring-and-candlestick/CAD_1.jpg 1200w&#34;&#xA;            sizes=&#34;(max-width: 500px) 500px, (max-width: 1000px) 1000px, 75vw&#34;&#xA;            src=&#34;https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-a-beginners-keyring-and-candlestick/CAD_1.jpg&#34;&#xA;            width=&#34;1200&#34;&#xA;            height=&#34;1600&#34;&#xA;            title=&#34;Cad 1&#34;&#xA;            alt=&#34;Cad 1&#34;&#xA;            loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;            fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/button&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Cad 1&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;div id=&#34;img-001&#34; popover&gt;&#xA;          &lt;img src=&#34;https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-a-beginners-keyring-and-candlestick/CAD_1.jpg&#34;&#xA;            title=&#34;Cad 1&#34;&#xA;            alt=&#34;Cad 1&#34;&#xA;            loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;            fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;button class=&#34;close&#34;&#xA;            popovertarget=&#34;img-001&#34;&#xA;            popovertargetaction=&#34;hide&#34;&#xA;            aria-label=&#34;Close image viewer&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;icon-cross&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M4 20 20 4M4 4 20 20&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;There&amp;rsquo;s a great phrase about education used in various communities &amp;ldquo;Each One Teach One&amp;rdquo;. Funnily enough I first noticed the phrase as it got used in the FreeCAD Twitter/X account as a hashtag. It&amp;rsquo;s rooted in African culture and initial usage was amongst enslaved people in America who, denied any education, would share what skills they had with their community.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Shawn Hymel discusses FreeCAD on the Amp Hour Podcast</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/shawn-hymel-discusses-freecad-on-the-amp-hour-podcast/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Aug 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/shawn-hymel-discusses-freecad-on-the-amp-hour-podcast/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;image-with-popover&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;figure&gt;&#xA;        &lt;button aria-label=&#34;Zoom image&#34; popovertarget=&#34;img-001&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;img srcset=&#34;https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/shawn-hymel-discusses-freecad-on-the-amp-hour-podcast/675-ShawnHymel_hu_751347d53d38abce.webp 500w, https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/shawn-hymel-discusses-freecad-on-the-amp-hour-podcast/675-ShawnHymel.jpg 768w&#34;&#xA;            sizes=&#34;(max-width: 500px) 500px, 75vw&#34;&#xA;            src=&#34;https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/shawn-hymel-discusses-freecad-on-the-amp-hour-podcast/675-ShawnHymel.jpg&#34;&#xA;            width=&#34;768&#34;&#xA;            height=&#34;768&#34;&#xA;            title=&#34;Shawn Hymel&#34;&#xA;            alt=&#34;Shawn Hymel&#34;&#xA;            loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;            fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/button&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Shawn Hymel&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;div id=&#34;img-001&#34; popover&gt;&#xA;          &lt;img src=&#34;https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/shawn-hymel-discusses-freecad-on-the-amp-hour-podcast/675-ShawnHymel.jpg&#34;&#xA;            title=&#34;Shawn Hymel&#34;&#xA;            alt=&#34;Shawn Hymel&#34;&#xA;            loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;            fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;button class=&#34;close&#34;&#xA;            popovertarget=&#34;img-001&#34;&#xA;            popovertargetaction=&#34;hide&#34;&#xA;            aria-label=&#34;Close image viewer&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;icon-cross&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M4 20 20 4M4 4 20 20&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Shawn Hymel recently appeared on the excellent Amp Hour podcast discussing some changes in direction in his work. Shawn is currently moving from his role in developer relations at Edge Impulse back towards creating training and educative content and course.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Forged in FreeCAD: Avian Hang Gliders</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-avian-hang-gliders/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 30 Jul 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-avian-hang-gliders/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Hang gliders are mesmerising when you see them in the sky. Silently cutting through the sky smoothly, often spotted in fine weather and in beautiful locations there&amp;rsquo;s a lot to be said for them. Over on fosstodon we&amp;rsquo;ve seen a UK based hang glide company &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.avianonline.co.uk/index.php?osCsid=1c2e1500a740b436df943e614dd407de&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Avian Hang Gliders &lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;mentioning how they use &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.freecad.org/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;FreeCAD&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; to develop their newest generation of gliders using clever simulation and advanced manufacturing techniques. We caught up with the owner of Avian, Tim Swait to chat about their process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Forged in FreeCAD: STEMFIE, 3D printable Open Source construction kit</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-stemfie-3d-printable-open-source-construction-kit/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 13 Jul 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-stemfie-3d-printable-open-source-construction-kit/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.stemfie.org/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;STEMFIE&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is an amazing, unique project that feels a little like an imaginative 3D printed hybrid of LEGO Mindstorms and Meccano. All the part designs are freely shared and available. This means people can 3D print locally building their own part collection, it&amp;rsquo;s mind boggling how many parts and projects there are!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Forged in FreeCAD: Boat hull hydrostatic and stability analysis</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-boat-hull-hydrostatic-and-stability-analysis/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 21 Jun 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-boat-hull-hydrostatic-and-stability-analysis/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Pretty much everyday someone somewhere is doing something spectacular with FreeCAD!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Spotted last week over on the&lt;a href=&#34;https://forum.freecad.org/viewtopic.php?t=88520&amp;amp;sid=b2d6cf127e3d87e02417b63d3cb8b845&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt; FreeCAD forum&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; BlueHorizon posted about a proof of concept project to model a boat hull and then perform a hydrostatic and stability analysis to work out how well the design performs.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
