    <item>
      <title>Forged In FreeCAD: 4Axis for CNC ring engraving</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-4axis-for-cnc-ring-engraving/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 14 May 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-4axis-for-cnc-ring-engraving/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;ve featured a few projects under the &amp;ldquo;Forged In FreeCAD&amp;rdquo; title but what caught our eye with this one is that FreeCAD was used to not only create an innovative solution, but also was used to then help operate the created machine.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Forged in FreeCAD: LumenPnP, an Open Source Pick and Place machine</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-lumenpnp-an-open-source-pick-and-place-machine/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 12 Apr 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-lumenpnp-an-open-source-pick-and-place-machine/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s an amazing age for making things, and an even greater age for making things using open source solutions. At our recent &lt;a href=&#34;https://blog.freecad.org/2024/02/16/fosdem-and-freecad-2024/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;FOSDEM&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; stand we shared the booth with &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.kicad.org/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;KiCad&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, the open source electronics environment. It was fabulous at the event to see items and machines made using KiCad and &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.freecad.org/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;FreeCAD&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; in combination. It&amp;rsquo;s also quite amazing to consider the complex printed circuit boards (PCB&amp;rsquo;s) KiCad can create with the tiny component packages placed and soldered into highly accurate positions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Meet Max: Working on Bug Triage</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/meet-max-working-on-bug-triage/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 22 Mar 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/meet-max-working-on-bug-triage/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Based in Germany, Max is a mechanical engineer in the automotive industry working on electric drive systems for vehicles. In his work life Catia seats are more the norm but Max was interested in alternatives he could use at home to fuel his passion for 3D printing. Of course this led Max to FreeCAD. Max has some lovely personal projects he has created using FreeCAD which you can check out over on &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.printables.com/@maxwxyz/models&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Max&amp;rsquo;s Printables Page&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Forged In FreeCAD: Angharad&#39;s bin repair</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-angharads-bin-repair/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 16 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-angharads-bin-repair/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;image-with-popover&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;figure&gt;&#xA;        &lt;button aria-label=&#34;Zoom image&#34; popovertarget=&#34;img-001&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;img srcset=&#34;https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-angharads-bin-repair/hinge-screenshot_hu_8c5322d42c25ebbd.webp 500w, https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-angharads-bin-repair/hinge-screenshot_hu_cb3c0abd709a38e5.webp 1000w, https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-angharads-bin-repair/hinge-screenshot.png 1014w&#34;&#xA;            sizes=&#34;(max-width: 500px) 500px, (max-width: 1000px) 1000px, 75vw&#34;&#xA;            src=&#34;https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-angharads-bin-repair/hinge-screenshot.png&#34;&#xA;            width=&#34;1014&#34;&#xA;            height=&#34;1798&#34;&#xA;            title=&#34;Hinge screenshot&#34;&#xA;            alt=&#34;Hinge screenshot&#34;&#xA;            loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;            fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/button&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Hinge screenshot&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;div id=&#34;img-001&#34; popover&gt;&#xA;          &lt;img src=&#34;https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-angharads-bin-repair/hinge-screenshot.png&#34;&#xA;            title=&#34;Hinge screenshot&#34;&#xA;            alt=&#34;Hinge screenshot&#34;&#xA;            loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;            fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;button class=&#34;close&#34;&#xA;            popovertarget=&#34;img-001&#34;&#xA;            popovertargetaction=&#34;hide&#34;&#xA;            aria-label=&#34;Close image viewer&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;icon-cross&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M4 20 20 4M4 4 20 20&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s wonderful to see people taking their first steps in CAD using FreeCAD and it&amp;rsquo;s even better when someone&amp;rsquo;s first project is to create something useful. In this case, new to FreeCAD Angharad, was motivated to learn to mend a faulty kitchen bin which she really liked.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Forged in FreeCAD: Alexander&#39;s PCB Holder</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-alexanders-pcb-holder/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Nov 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-alexanders-pcb-holder/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Spotted over on Mastodon, we thought Alexander&amp;rsquo;s (AKA &lt;a href=&#34;https://mastodon.online/@PistonPin&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;@PistonPin&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) PCB holder design was an excellent tool and a great example of functional 3D printing and FreeCAD. Chatting with Alexander it&amp;rsquo;s clear he is an experienced CAD user with lots of previous projects under his belt.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Forged In FreeCAD: Erika&#39;s &#39;Not a Moon&#39;</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-erikas-not-a-moon/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 09 Nov 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/forged-in-freecad-erikas-not-a-moon/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Spotted online, FreeCAD user &lt;a href=&#34;https://twitter.com/erikaheidi/status/1719071492791521344&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Erika Heidi&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was keen to explore sketching on round surfaces using the &lt;a href=&#34;https://wiki.freecad.org/Curves_Workbench&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Curves WB&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. As a fan of Star Wars her learning project leaned into the idea of a desktop death star as a small desktop organiser box. It&amp;rsquo;s a lovely object and a great example of sketching onto near spherical objects.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>A Research Grade Open Source Microscope</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/a-research-grade-open-source-microscope-made-with-freecad/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 13 Feb 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/a-research-grade-open-source-microscope-made-with-freecad/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The PUMA microscope is a low cost, modular, 3D printed, open source microscope designed in FreeCAD. Its modular nature allows re-use of many components to reconfigure the scope into a multitude of possible forms, from a basic mirror-illuminated simple microscope (middle) to a complex scope for serious research applications (right) - while still being fully portable!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
